# Normalize source to LF in the repository, whatever the checkout platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Flight logs are binary, whatever their extension says.
#
# Git's text heuristics see ".TXT" and rewrite line endings on a Windows
# checkout. For a log that is fatal rather than cosmetic: every 0x0A inside
# encoded frame data becomes 0x0D 0x0A, which changes the file's length and
# desynchronizes the frame stream. This was caught by a fixture whose committed
# length was 1224 bytes and whose Windows checkout was 1241 — exactly the 17
# newlines in its header.
fixtures/** -text
*.TXT -text
*.bbl -text
*.bfl -text
*.BBL -text
*.BFL -text

# The Gradle wrapper. gradlew.bat is run by cmd.exe, which needs CRLF line
# endings for its label/goto handling; the global `* text=auto eol=lf` above
# would otherwise strip them on checkout and break the script on Windows.
*.bat        text eol=crlf
gradlew      text eol=lf
*.jar        binary

# Patch artifacts preserve upstream diff context byte-for-byte. Check their
# applied result with `git apply --whitespace=error-all`, not the outer diff.
integration/rotorflight-firmware/**/*.patch -whitespace
